    "gallery": "All four preserved examples meet this quiet-final-year event; they are unrepresentative of its frequency in an unbiased prior ensemble.",
    "law": "Zero-origin lognormal rough variance is not mean-reverting: mean(V_t|theta)=xi_0(t), while median(V_t|theta)=xi_0(t)*exp(-eta^2*q_grid(t)/2). The typical level therefore changes with model age.",
    "case_variation": "Fixed parameters do not fix the realized path. For case 3 the event occurred in only 2 of 512 new independent paths.",
    "numerical": "No zeros, nonfinite values, subnormal values, variance floor, clipping or rejected/redrawn paths in the audited rough ensembles. The direct Gaussian hybrid compensator exactly matches its grid variance.",
    "mean_warning": "Analytic conditional mean is fixed by the exact Gaussian compensator; bounded ordinary Monte Carlo cannot certify heavy-tailed means. Empirical mean SE may miss rare tail mass; theoretical moments are reported separately.",
    "lesson_limit": "This is a generative-model setup limitation for stationary long-run physical returns, not evidence that every rough path dies out. A stationary or mean-reverting rough alternative would require a new task, training and validation."
  },
